ate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38fd4660-39ca-585f-8e3a-5d8b569be77d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161041/selection/f6a9267c4876e367957281e0c19b0f2bef7aa2178ddb192eb718125886e8e2fb" :answer/id #uuid "efddd605-9598-5cd4-94c2-83344d6e00c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(r+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161041/selection/4605dbb72f1a6173e37a4f79d89f6e2d1bbc10ba6292ecb2785f1574cd62fb88" :answer/id #uuid "8798f949-be5c-590e-8c96-7d2dce3cc42c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161041/selection/91dccb817c1d9007123a4d27d8bbfcacb105f35775f45a5d2cd85131472afd5e" :answer/id #uuid "606c8332-bba6-58db-9a78-9442e5188dff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{16}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(r+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161041/selection/42f3718a06e9eff0b5f71c7177effa336f0887abb8be066ee6ea13d0c61e542c" :answer/id #uuid "24d9ab24-3434-5367-9c12-36aea284e362" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161041/selection/b7fbd7a29dbec2d0b3ad827f11baef928154e8e68951bb95d153e90b7063cb33" :answer/id #uuid "1c9ab42f-4b67-5cde-978d-afbbfb028f20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161041/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "92bdd188-4aa7-591e-9ebd-a0b3c08b2c0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161041/selection/42f3718a06e9eff0b5f71c7177effa336f0887abb8be066ee6ea13d0c61e542c" :answer-field/choices ["q-161041/selection/f6a9267c4876e367957281e0c19b0f2bef7aa2178ddb192eb718125886e8e2fb" "q-161041/selection/4605dbb72f1a6173e37a4f79d89f6e2d1bbc10ba6292ecb2785f1574cd62fb88" "q-161041/selection/91dccb817c1d9007123a4d27d8bbfcacb105f35775f45a5d2cd85131472afd5e" "q-161041/selection/42f3718a06e9eff0b5f71c7177effa336f0887abb8be066ee6ea13d0c61e542c" "q-161041/selection/b7fbd7a29dbec2d0b3ad827f11baef928154e8e68951bb95d153e90b7063cb33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161041" :question/id #uuid "a368d06f-dd38-5739-a1e1-1669cc437d2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161041" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/6b077d20bcb79f293383a7810d1c46ad42ce78d17a8d631b01f66a9fd547f475.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the circle shown above. What is ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $4$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\operatorname{ln}⁡((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+1)r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+1)\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38fd4660-39ca-585f-8e3a-5d8b569be77d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38076"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/bccbe3973fa63908f5e264f4566e1207c5019dc1de9c36ef42481428527aef3b.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the semicircle shown above. What is\n${∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A$\nexpressed in polar coordinates?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $2$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-83502/selection/58ad8afc2125ce45256b799f6646fa6c3ad55883f92fc3d5170d977c7cafb950" :answer/id #uuid "1dde174c-33d8-531d-a172-31b732845323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83502/selection/40c38d3db60279a016d9e129aba5d44354f1846365e103fb299d8fec881e1b6c" :answer/id #uuid "1dfc901b-0da8-5655-948e-62d1ea2a163f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83502/selection/a39642b38b2b1b9d7a2800c9247d6d7a501f34599ba7435c1bc29400e7a4355a" :answer/id #uuid "30b150bf-dd68-57d6-bb9a-dd3320e867dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83502/selection/bddd9e92b653392ac5aa2337bfa36396258cf1dbfac89e7e3ac11c72ea27c70a" :answer/id #uuid "e82b5f1d-2abf-58ff-8736-3a42dfa44eb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83502/selection/e69191cf91ba3136872abe84e387c3661497986534dfc3fa7dcffaef20aa25b6" :answer/id #uuid "dc7f1e1b-0c3a-59c4-8c06-e032562bd0e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83502/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a56ff3-c38e-5ca8-910d-99a3a6ad00be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83502/selection/58ad8afc2125ce45256b799f6646fa6c3ad55883f92fc3d5170d977c7cafb950" :answer-field/choices ["q-83502/selection/58ad8afc2125ce45256b799f6646fa6c3ad55883f92fc3d5170d977c7cafb950" "q-83502/selection/40c38d3db60279a016d9e129aba5d44354f1846365e103fb299d8fec881e1b6c" "q-83502/selection/a39642b38b2b1b9d7a2800c9247d6d7a501f34599ba7435c1bc29400e7a4355a" "q-83502/selection/bddd9e92b653392ac5aa2337bfa36396258cf1dbfac89e7e3ac11c72ea27c70a" "q-83502/selection/e69191cf91ba3136872abe84e387c3661497986534dfc3fa7dcffaef20aa25b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83502" :question/id #uuid "25c3bb11-298f-5171-a671-9a16a5376e88" :question/math-academy-id "q-83502" :question/problem "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}\\le 4,\\,x\\ge 0},$ then ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/968419bad65410864c75e8abe766d21ac4d4acd835c73ea84118cf21ac066f79.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $2$ centered at $(0,2).$ \n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -4r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4 & =4 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-4r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-4r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/2fe33fb6e1be8b6107cb667e9453613af906bd4da7d67f9d9323d49cce5ae06c.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =0$ (the positive $x$-axis) and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (the positive $y$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/e2b5e7b4433cbfb50ac7a9f991e4e4bc0cf8deecfefeeef0a4c9606ab6183cce.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\sqrt{{r}^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83502/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1091c5-d81a-565f-a281-b2fb0d00c973"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83502"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83956/selection/800942bbbd5d244954a79e93c3e27b3a46bf66d1bb0814ab6e10b5ff25ffcb27" :answer/id #uuid "5150cf74-5fba-5b5a-8934-35cc013a95fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83956/selection/090c3dd3f538321e057b664c38662dc9ef98c49ba8354111feaf4ae9491914d0" :answer/id #uuid "370e9a0b-8d3b-5262-91c8-f39c45055b51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }2r\\operatorname{ln}⁡(r+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83956/selection/219e60dbd8389c5470b64b168f4f442fe697266a42bef93eef1f45465eccdbf6" :answer/id #uuid "bd933dbb-b8ca-5b21-b9a8-6e26f66089d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(r+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83956/selection/a755928befa1ab73108dc69d4952c041d0489aade61c7e56db852ecffa02d8f4" :answer/id #uuid "e2d0514d-0a4d-597e-8b1a-611f3716d3fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2})\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83956/selection/8b48a2483067600221ad902cf9c5ff42f6becab8e65a7ba4b6c73a601ca734ac" :answer/id #uuid "1939b458-ee9a-577d-a301-6fcf3158d55d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83956/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a7ab112-561c-58a7-8791-3ca05d91069a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83956/selection/800942bbbd5d244954a79e93c3e27b3a46bf66d1bb0814ab6e10b5ff25ffcb27" :answer-field/choices ["q-83956/selection/800942bbbd5d244954a79e93c3e27b3a46bf66d1bb0814ab6e10b5ff25ffcb27" "q-83956/selection/090c3dd3f538321e057b664c38662dc9ef98c49ba8354111feaf4ae9491914d0" "q-83956/selection/219e60dbd8389c5470b64b168f4f442fe697266a42bef93eef1f45465eccdbf6" "q-83956/selection/a755928befa1ab73108dc69d4952c041d0489aade61c7e56db852ecffa02d8f4" "q-83956/selection/8b48a2483067600221ad902cf9c5ff42f6becab8e65a7ba4b6c73a601ca734ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83956" :question/id #uuid "b1de76f2-2bbf-5f6f-8001-65ebe80eec1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-83956" :question/problem "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1,\\,y\\le 0},$ then ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/bf84eed655256e63439ca907610c4b0b022c6c480d5ab0b6c12d6826af9f0907.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at $(1,0).$ \n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1)^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/6de2b6e2b9925577f8cf0961f8466707f770ddca175a04dac9b592542aac16e8.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (the negative $y$-axis) and $\\theta =0$ (the positive $x$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/4a56d4023b03b40b4c1be5f22809963d6c745fd90ed3d860cf69d555b3e869ae.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 0}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\operatorname{ln}⁡((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+1)\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83956/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1091c5-d81a-565f-a281-b2fb0d00c973"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83956"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161070/selection/d3141f6aa051e5ad5fa7e6dd6fd66a4005098bf467ceb9651e36302e8a0a813a" :answer/id #uuid "aab06e08-c4ff-5c66-991d-76170f18503c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161070/selection/953944b8528e0b1292be397e6009b2958172fd7732617218257a2c21e6a85cc5" :answer/id #uuid "8955dbe3-728d-50b5-967a-0f86ce8db534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{e}^{{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161070/selection/9c27d234fcd419996ac43325afea025e574b97b74027142804c8211e096e1e70" :answer/id #uuid "dc594d31-cd3b-5bc7-92dc-c3f85446d09f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161070/selection/b3cf80084d9a726e193c3a8f73ff7d7d72b1872da74b625a85fa1ffa47584723" :answer/id #uuid "3cb6dd65-54f3-59d4-b149-93bf3731d588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161070/selection/71beba41890c042dffce011f22d5e89d36e6baace4a1e342d0b63663f880d2f9" :answer/id #uuid "fd3fe763-66c1-5fdb-b766-52af73c71b01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r{e}^{{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161070/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "841678aa-ed99-5826-8d93-1f95492f0269" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161070/selection/71beba41890c042dffce011f22d5e89d36e6baace4a1e342d0b63663f880d2f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-161070/selection/d3141f6aa051e5ad5fa7e6dd6fd66a4005098bf467ceb9651e36302e8a0a813a" "q-161070/selection/953944b8528e0b1292be397e6009b2958172fd7732617218257a2c21e6a85cc5" "q-161070/selection/9c27d234fcd419996ac43325afea025e574b97b74027142804c8211e096e1e70" "q-161070/selection/b3cf80084d9a726e193c3a8f73ff7d7d72b1872da74b625a85fa1ffa47584723" "q-161070/selection/71beba41890c042dffce011f22d5e89d36e6baace4a1e342d0b63663f880d2f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161070" :question/id #uuid "15d5d84c-a45c-5cae-a9ee-05c1c4659504" :question/math-academy-id "q-161070" :question/problem "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 16,\\,y\\le 0},$ then ${∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/d882bf70ecb7b94eee0eeeffbf63874ca8607268167f96278deb4678ec3b827a.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $4$ centered at $(4,0).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=16$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4)}^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +16+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =16 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/55c9ea38874993dd10f03061fc3739ec6d7cb8af5b0467d5060a74a5ec22393a.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (the negative $y$-axis) and $\\theta =0$ (the positive $x$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/b845816016bbc646e88af59bd02602b2e1127edfbc22ca82d1fb4e52cc63b41a.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r{e}^{{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r{e}^{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r{e}^{{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161070/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1091c5-d81a-565f-a281-b2fb0d00c973"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83501/selection/5d5c3817b740c68d14ff61831ecaefd08b5931dccd286a54bce96c63e2727793" :answer/id #uuid "618e6e8b-220f-54c3-ac8b-0b534cca51c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83501/selection/7a1bb40c56fd712d100110e16f660b70593e2349583ed1abade55442a5d87430" :answer/id #uuid "e8c5ccbd-26a5-5a70-943a-8a399e60c4c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83501/selection/62ca9b0a8318a09f5179175ba8dc6c017dc324859835bccc6f9e2ae7848ee400" :answer/id #uuid "03454402-1b43-52d7-b7fd-e510ee964b47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83501/selection/af71264b9eca05c9ecbf856df8bf0b1fd623983e36d4e0a46a6330623bd1cae6" :answer/id #uuid "4b53ade8-df86-5738-ae0b-4f9b6bdfe796" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83501/selection/86e739ec8cade7bad1eaed43d6644e18dcaca30e3ea9689d771d178cef006330" :answer/id #uuid "b70faa86-94ee-5db4-bd04-f670a404d586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83501/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "626860ae-5b94-5ef9-95f4-f7d64ad8cedb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83501/selection/af71264b9eca05c9ecbf856df8bf0b1fd623983e36d4e0a46a6330623bd1cae6" :answer-field/choices ["q-83501/selection/5d5c3817b740c68d14ff61831ecaefd08b5931dccd286a54bce96c63e2727793" "q-83501/selection/7a1bb40c56fd712d100110e16f660b70593e2349583ed1abade55442a5d87430" "q-83501/selection/62ca9b0a8318a09f5179175ba8dc6c017dc324859835bccc6f9e2ae7848ee400" "q-83501/selection/af71264b9eca05c9ecbf856df8bf0b1fd623983e36d4e0a46a6330623bd1cae6" "q-83501/selection/86e739ec8cade7bad1eaed43d6644e18dcaca30e3ea9689d771d178cef006330"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83501" :question/id #uuid "f578d29d-0823-5f21-864f-baa92f133476" :question/math-academy-id "q-83501" :question/problem "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4},\\,y\\le 0},$ then ${∬}_{D}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/617a69d44661d03e1c170b0c397d11f6437a7222c286df5023154371ec90ab4d.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\frac{1}{2}$ centered at $(-\\frac{1}{2},0).$ \n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}+r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$ \n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/fe82880fec605db684a2b5cb0da5c88a38da5b4fb4faad1f80c4d5b0691fde21.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =\\pi $ (the negative $x$-axis) and $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ (the negative $y$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/9e1693005c8930a7b2b8a3b47bc96f5441bf72ee6c5b67f3b8c97d87cfa2e34b.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83501/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1091c5-d81a-565f-a281-b2fb0d00c973"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83501"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161067/selection/3afab6b7a19799fa7288d31eb81d19a5688645786970f3659cf88a0728929b50" :answer/id #uuid "3d40782e-845e-5270-a0b3-32751174dde1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161067/selection/15db5b2816a3959080e052db0e9560ed4f9d1a063fb56bad83a13df34718bbe3" :answer/id #uuid "2e202ec4-69a6-5c64-967e-f7b790b69117" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161067/selection/c788568abea2ba5b64ffd74a62b5a2a8873fdce359822269ac82d0e48c9b75e8" :answer/id #uuid "c285bf83-963f-58b2-98c4-a67cad83c6c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161067/selection/3707d06656737e0f4011dd5004aceffb413a55fd9d412058b594b619f324eda2" :answer/id #uuid "708f0b62-e1fb-5d2d-90d1-7dd7624fea8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161067/selection/2d67e05c9f4c09fbbae50a2663f52bf6b55eb1151b42932eb79b7e641352c044" :answer/id #uuid "f5861a77-b52d-5232-820c-f6feac1f1a7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161067/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "91e3b0ea-da7f-59db-a664-d8845c12044c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161067/selection/15db5b2816a3959080e052db0e9560ed4f9d1a063fb56bad83a13df34718bbe3" :answer-field/choices ["q-161067/selection/3afab6b7a19799fa7288d31eb81d19a5688645786970f3659cf88a0728929b50" "q-161067/selection/15db5b2816a3959080e052db0e9560ed4f9d1a063fb56bad83a13df34718bbe3" "q-161067/selection/c788568abea2ba5b64ffd74a62b5a2a8873fdce359822269ac82d0e48c9b75e8" "q-161067/selection/3707d06656737e0f4011dd5004aceffb413a55fd9d412058b594b619f324eda2" "q-161067/selection/2d67e05c9f4c09fbbae50a2663f52bf6b55eb1151b42932eb79b7e641352c044"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161067" :question/id #uuid "27f89428-72cb-554a-ae1c-3b9c76fc7457" :question/math-academy-id "q-161067" :question/problem "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4},$ then ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/86036fd86096355b969da695f812c9bf835880edd68f7991183b70a6234e3eb4.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $2$ centered at $(2,0).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2)}^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =4 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/0cf12dd41cddb943fe8b0950cdf13a0480cfbf2620a59d8bc4e8ba8775e0e6c1.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (the negative $y$-axis) and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (the positive $y$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/cf2f0a011734a56f59cce2164a82d745c84b28d1bf706531deb80bb6e0a32640.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161067/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1091c5-d81a-565f-a281-b2fb0d00c973"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161067"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83958/selection/1ac63dccee3a9ca710e0753cddb1476a5e3dd8c56531412c905ad5107908ccb9" :answer/id #uuid "a6aea106-16af-5439-8eaa-640398bf801d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83958/selection/9f3dd3ca48b76bdf90c3ef7c201e95d54034cb03aa2b850c233dd8c22787ddbe" :answer/id #uuid "c5caec59-c0e6-5684-96ad-7332a90c802b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83958/selection/d912b1df032f45438aaa0d1988903a06417f3fd06148f15c8b0192802f02304d" :answer/id #uuid "d5dad718-0243-5b74-87cd-e9661853a032" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4-\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83958/selection/b5be7d38503dcbf1896dc73e5bd6ccf72db0ba1c926b6910aad76337483f2ff5" :answer/id #uuid "3ebcbde6-7c2f-5d7b-9b37-174ebb3dabbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83958/selection/3a34935d43335ad5c2f1b8007b57c0dbcfc95a2a2c6c04f10e1e14261515d9c2" :answer/id #uuid "3bc53d08-9820-50ba-95c6-41de93bdd75e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8-\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83958/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a579482-1200-5103-807a-0f355a547f65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83958/selection/3a34935d43335ad5c2f1b8007b57c0dbcfc95a2a2c6c04f10e1e14261515d9c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-83958/selection/1ac63dccee3a9ca710e0753cddb1476a5e3dd8c56531412c905ad5107908ccb9" "q-83958/selection/9f3dd3ca48b76bdf90c3ef7c201e95d54034cb03aa2b850c233dd8c22787ddbe" "q-83958/selection/d912b1df032f45438aaa0d1988903a06417f3fd06148f15c8b0192802f02304d" "q-83958/selection/b5be7d38503dcbf1896dc73e5bd6ccf72db0ba1c926b6910aad76337483f2ff5" "q-83958/selection/3a34935d43335ad5c2f1b8007b57c0dbcfc95a2a2c6c04f10e1e14261515d9c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83958" :question/id #uuid "bd160ee6-138a-522e-a95d-3e2bceb3df15" :question/math-academy-id "q-83958" :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }^{1}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }^{1}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]_{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}({1}^{2}-(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{4}\\theta -\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{8-\\pi }{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83958/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83958"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161049/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "7a8cf782-21ef-523d-967a-e369b47fe1de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161049/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "bbe1a2c5-7932-5ffc-827f-79531ac0ad9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161049/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "88e3cab4-531b-5ba0-8a96-e77c3d18357e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161049/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c8385f19-0b30-51ec-a95b-90c37db36b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161049/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "46155b0d-ec48-56c1-bd0d-992e26d32015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161049/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8539fa9-465b-549c-a960-cd0862f91f9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161049/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-161049/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-161049/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-161049/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-161049/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-161049/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161049" :question/id #uuid "512462da-282b-58d8-8c7f-36bc1ec6079f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161049" :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{sin}^{3}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\frac{1}{3}{sin}^{3}⁡0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[(1-\\frac{1}{3})-0] \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161049/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83511/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "2e9855b2-6ead-50a0-bcac-4fc6a99978eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83511/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "991e8489-55d7-5cb8-bae5-bde61d3ce0e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83511/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a801b704-44c6-51bf-86d6-8be8633ec270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83511/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "ec55f09e-26c7-5367-a6d8-14cb16109c05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83511/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" :answer/id #uuid "cb4d1b1a-e066-5a67-8b6d-2d63426ca663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83511/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad30e96f-4217-54ce-9262-85db065517e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83511/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-83511/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-83511/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-83511/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-83511/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-83511/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83511" :question/id #uuid "a2871775-3209-5197-a973-f8e607320739" :question/math-academy-id "q-83511" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ({3}^{4}-{1}^{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =20{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =20[\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2}]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =10{[{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =10({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{sin}^{2}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =10(1-0) \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83511/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83511"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38031"] :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }2r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,[{r}^{2}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{1}^{3}-{0}^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-83957/selection/7b88eb253dea651c281f0e0e5363fa88cbcf300715926c0a6791d454277562dc" :answer/id #uuid "b4475a94-6f8a-5eb8-91d0-80d8fa7f11ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83957/selection/8799e02886d0a392717cf567e84a29c882cb3e2ecf8acdc4fcf1c78ab4d29f97" :answer/id #uuid "9a67518c-9b16-533b-bfdf-104346ab4309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83957/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "1a940b97-0fa4-5b58-ad89-e610559ad7d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83957/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c426dd52-b17a-5dc9-b7ef-80de664fd6e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83957/selection/5ff07dfc191981282085a25f57933292db094aa2d2460ca5de1190abd8b453df" :answer/id #uuid "ebba41a1-6840-5d03-81a1-030977e925d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83957/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "274b8996-5f96-58b1-947c-32beefa51d09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83957/selection/8799e02886d0a392717cf567e84a29c882cb3e2ecf8acdc4fcf1c78ab4d29f97" :answer-field/choices ["q-83957/selection/7b88eb253dea651c281f0e0e5363fa88cbcf300715926c0a6791d454277562dc" "q-83957/selection/8799e02886d0a392717cf567e84a29c882cb3e2ecf8acdc4fcf1c78ab4d29f97" "q-83957/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" "q-83957/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-83957/selection/5ff07dfc191981282085a25f57933292db094aa2d2460ca5de1190abd8b453df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83957" :question/id #uuid "4914f088-4f0d-5ca8-84e7-acd24daf7336" :question/math-academy-id "q-83957" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{2}^{4}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =6[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]_{\\pi /6}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83957/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83957"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38140"] :question/problem "Integrate the function $f(x,y)=2x+y$ over the portion of the disk of radius $2$ centered at the origin, where $y\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/b5ba69ab02aa13e201b7b9113f6a36e705ad19e6412499504afc4f239459a8f3.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(2x+y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ){\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,{[\\frac{{r}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}((2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161055/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "eff0d9f0-e8fc-58ae-bf00-fd167038818c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161055/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "01d133f2-26de-58da-ba8a-53d3dd75dd9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161055/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "d82e343e-9dc8-5f46-baae-940630014471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161055/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9ce93789-5f77-5945-ab9f-f4e00ad6ffd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161055/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0cefc46c-2881-5719-b445-ea73ebcb8faa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161055/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eda02526-a3f5-5c6a-a71f-6207f3616233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161055/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-161055/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" "q-161055/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-161055/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" "q-161055/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-161055/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161055" :question/id #uuid "06e5e252-a3f4-5add-b589-60c1a81d21b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161055" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/719f86db69489f62bcbe2753e88cdc6713f04dc6f53415cc2484e2eaab8ffac3.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where the region $D$ is the semicircle shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at \n$(0,1).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $x=\\sqrt{2y-{y}^{2}}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{2y-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =2y-{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2y \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTherefore, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }(2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-1-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161055/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b97f75d-c784-5f3a-984d-f9a5fdf21d61"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161055"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161050/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "6eb533b3-aa61-5d47-acd1-05b4a4d95533" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161050/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "36ffc6fb-fc3e-5633-a610-c28cfcfecb82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161050/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "2d8f6b75-64f1-5d2d-ad3d-d011814a23ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161050/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "898ea8d8-a31f-5f9f-aa39-cada8e2e9dd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161050/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5fa1ed26-2194-5f41-a964-ca650534cdc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161050/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe171bab-14f7-5ed8-80fa-7fc7628acca2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161050/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-161050/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-161050/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-161050/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-161050/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-161050/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161050" :question/id #uuid "f1d73d5b-dabc-5deb-b03b-6ee0e0496e2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161050" :question/problem "Integrate the function $f(x,y)=15{x}^{2}y$ over the disk of radius $1$ centered at the origin." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/9b54b7a488a1983ba1816fdf5c55e039951eb417102c61963977b2f48b9c8d9e.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}12{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}15({r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}15{r}^{4}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ){\\int }_{0}^{1}5{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,{[{r}^{5}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(1-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =[-{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta ]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-({cos}^{3}⁡(2\\pi )-{cos}^{3}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161050/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b97f75d-c784-5f3a-984d-f9a5fdf21d61"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161050"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161053/selection/6d0126c2995f99db2161220c4df0bb9432204dbfd9d81c4994846b5139bff8ae" :answer/id #uuid "5666d663-a872-5f22-8900-37d9083b35c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi ({e}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161053/selection/a3b38038062cad8421c9d734443b1525581995352db8538c5842a3ca3b5961d6" :answer/id #uuid "faa850ca-177a-57d8-bf46-122dc07a5996" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}(2\\pi -1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161053/selection/a9237b9bdbf6f674586f1127d2c08290d89362e8393d239817177d197d1a5654" :answer/id #uuid "b4a13fa4-69e5-5c9c-be34-91f4cc8cdb75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi ({e}^{4}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161053/selection/4da2737b6802e2aba625d8ac73d592025441af07deadfa5aa2fbdfc7cc3d55c1" :answer/id #uuid "82007ff4-2f27-5eae-b2c5-d908082b3108" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {e}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161053/selection/f6cd7ad815cbceebfe1cddfb3219edf7d8bce0273da1c741fc6acf433fc7d1c8" :answer/id #uuid "cfc0c378-9d0f-5fc6-9342-7014ed611d41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161053/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cd7750a-41e4-5307-8fa6-0ec9b5e35280" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161053/selection/a9237b9bdbf6f674586f1127d2c08290d89362e8393d239817177d197d1a5654" :answer-field/choices ["q-161053/selection/6d0126c2995f99db2161220c4df0bb9432204dbfd9d81c4994846b5139bff8ae" "q-161053/selection/a3b38038062cad8421c9d734443b1525581995352db8538c5842a3ca3b5961d6" "q-161053/selection/a9237b9bdbf6f674586f1127d2c08290d89362e8393d239817177d197d1a5654" "q-161053/selection/4da2737b6802e2aba625d8ac73d592025441af07deadfa5aa2fbdfc7cc3d55c1" "q-161053/selection/f6cd7ad815cbceebfe1cddfb3219edf7d8bce0273da1c741fc6acf433fc7d1c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161053" :question/id #uuid "566879ac-9f1e-5e9f-ad0e-aa10b226dd89" :question/math-academy-id "q-161053" :question/problem "Integrate the function $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ over the disk of radius $2$ centered at the origin." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/811cfa127ad232e8d5a990998604718a57344d1bd7f43173dc0987631c13db33.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{(r{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}r{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{r}^{2}}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{4}-1)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{4}-1)[\\theta ]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{4}-1)(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =\\pi ({e}^{4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161053/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b97f75d-c784-5f3a-984d-f9a5fdf21d61"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161053"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161054/selection/01bbf8ebd5069470431f8452e98a426e151975cb8793ee4f306144a87060a9a3" :answer/id #uuid "94287c6e-5f22-59ba-939c-a5439cb4048d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161054/selection/3fe0c2782ef9d49a7200cf08ec6a2381610c8be6c4d087640d3d1aa242e684c3" :answer/id #uuid "139dc11b-3cb7-5f75-a8d6-a83f49a88e39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161054/selection/f4a5418fa9b8fff0ce59279b550e49562ce305e66de4cc1871ab38c81ed94141" :answer/id #uuid "b4b89e1b-8bf8-5290-b472-f2ee3755eec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi -3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161054/selection/5f2764a3b43d99710592dc2bfba64e621c1d013a2188b17537546512dbbcd9de" :answer/id #uuid "b7501a2f-cd2e-5205-a315-fc3d65415a55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\pi +2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161054/selection/90db7e50123f93e0e45998c4ad0bb485a30665aa29f0b12dde8b1840a9ab5183" :answer/id #uuid "55ea357a-637c-56f7-8326-50029fc1f454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161054/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "40ef08fa-60ea-5a02-ab50-7f90ab741943" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161054/selection/3fe0c2782ef9d49a7200cf08ec6a2381610c8be6c4d087640d3d1aa242e684c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-161054/selection/01bbf8ebd5069470431f8452e98a426e151975cb8793ee4f306144a87060a9a3" "q-161054/selection/3fe0c2782ef9d49a7200cf08ec6a2381610c8be6c4d087640d3d1aa242e684c3" "q-161054/selection/f4a5418fa9b8fff0ce59279b550e49562ce305e66de4cc1871ab38c81ed94141" "q-161054/selection/5f2764a3b43d99710592dc2bfba64e621c1d013a2188b17537546512dbbcd9de" "q-161054/selection/90db7e50123f93e0e45998c4ad0bb485a30665aa29f0b12dde8b1840a9ab5183"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161054" :question/id #uuid "3ab5f3e7-d687-595f-9290-06218d674ab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161054" :question/problem "Integrate the function $f(x,y)=2({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ over the disk of radius $3$ centered at the origin" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/0a1de805051eff4ea82b4eefb7bb113c724b3d4e7304704831b6294ee4e4d674.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2({(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2})\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}2{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{∬}_{Δ}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,{[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(\\frac{81}{4}-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}[\\theta ]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =81\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161054/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b97f75d-c784-5f3a-984d-f9a5fdf21d61"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7347"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/1782385c55493892be0308ede1e4fbe5308ea9440e21b70cc2da7d7f01fb8dcd.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the quarter-circle shown above. What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D y \\sqrt{x^2+y^2} \\: \\textrm{d}A$\nexpressed in polar coordinates?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} f(x,y) \\ \\mathrm d A = \\iint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\ f(r\\cos\\theta, r\\sin\\theta) \\:  r \\ \\mathrm d r \\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r, \\theta),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\Delta = \\Big\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\Big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12376"] :question/problem "Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/f3007b053a76b455c6c5b7ea617039780e6ee7b856ac2c54ae124dad334aef7f.png) express the following integral in polar coordinates:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/5c67d939121c919b3d51b562efbc774a6f2a702d2a8e9cadee508446f9bd35d0.png)" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/7f645c475debdf46d06a9ecbebb3f019a7a92ea0c6129e06b8b5f326e005f9f6.png)\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/c592260e19248a715187208d54cafc6f4ceac8f34c843f1b366134bc37fb5430.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/e447e688e0f3e2c0411129e8d1baf4a900008173443f5392d98af52a27eb285b.png)\n\nNotice that the region ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/33d4430552670d83a2c303e8ab286d3391f5611450f4e4f0b6ad6ccb58049b0e.png) represents the disk of radius ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/f7b723906930985b61bc58989f341d6b2e1e1f70ff34946ce5f5f373e2b0f95a.png) centered at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/484ceb02ac6fd60fc3d18cfff327672d25f5b88cb1b1825b8c1e069f153b9545.png) \n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/00dbdb2d8638277969db40d2ca7c43266b4f275fbeadee86f6ef37954661433b.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/b78de9de64536b59ded324af0c67d84d3d64802a8a8d1af3894abfc686e2ae53.png) in polar coordinates:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/185d596ce2824cf09bf7e5e7fd4cc432b75dfbe442c2e653564d93f347acf7ee.png) \n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/427fd471dcf18cc90c67eb53f8f20e484fa707110281ad49811bc6a4f2ed5968.png) cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/f560ba12327ee0ad0c69dbd656ab82ac974acf442e8a1642dcf597f340d7f6db.png)\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/427fd471dcf18cc90c67eb53f8f20e484fa707110281ad49811bc6a4f2ed5968.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/4302d6f15afc8636ab514cdce845f4bbe0171d743153ee6bdfbbe2b323bf4ac4.png) First of all, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/15012c54ccf6548b6c3e2201e44d9ccfd33d7d41c627a0ce22c56f4c6d41d16c.png) can vary from ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/4efe6d0d575bd5dd59ca5e6e05092a1d2030164be2ce65efd468d385e931fddb.png) (at the origin) to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/cecc5f8feb56bb745748bbc79f2bfdc884364e7b9dce2c027c8c251366bb6f32.png) (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/f5ff820a0def58e4a2e6b15b5b77368151a71a72a083ef92fd95c20dacf711d3.png)\n\nSecondly, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/e10bbbc0bc5b9cc38adb59e4daa0cd709a3d7165da31914f73e17bf28cc01902.png) can vary between ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/a55c0db211022b11f154d509c19b94022e218e9bf3120144dc2464bf5ca5c29c.png) (the negative ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/245bebfeb6cb95babe872c0185e33d598fb9dd08c8950252c07cdb5f5c8f87d4.png)-axis) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/bc5b0c56a73784c1d673cae720a8d7796922204eb07796b954ff10b197fea2c1.png) (the positive ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/245bebfeb6cb95babe872c0185e33d598fb9dd08c8950252c07cdb5f5c8f87d4.png)-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/c1e5fea69b62b94b565607da8d372160cc51dc127973f2afa4dda8cfc01116ea.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/7eff2673c3d979c233082bd82d26977e80eec3963f1ff142a4f3a7c63ef89790.png) the region can be expressed as \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/e20685d2d0ab9822cb380f6e5ddf2cf41a24bcc1d5c28b903b77b1c660e347cd.png)\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/92792892be94c40c231d24839bf521ea22dce3d4fd809cfc46b7d4312ebd5d4d.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7346"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\pi/8} \\int_0^{\\sin2\\theta} r \\, \\textrm d r\\,\\textrm d \\theta.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{[{r}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the double-angle formula\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} = 1-2\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2\\theta$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin^22\\theta = \\dfrac12\\left(1-\\cos4\\theta\\right).\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we can finish our integral by integrating with respect to $\\theta,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\theta -\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(0-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{2}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(\\pi -2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7348"] :question/problem "Integrate the function $f(x, y) = 15xy^2$ over the portion of the disk of radius $2$ centered at the origin, where $x \\geq 0,y \\geq 0.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} f(x,y) \\ \\mathrm d A = \\iint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\ f(r\\cos\\theta, r\\sin\\theta) \\:  r \\ \\mathrm d r \\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054995/assets/051cfbbf3fd37f01ff7e4442fccdc5ec4ce506e3c452b68bfa2ed5ae6e5cf6b9.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r, \\theta),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\Delta = \\left\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 2, \\:0\\leq \\theta \\leq  \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}15x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}15r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}15{r}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{2}5{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{[{r}^{5}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ({2}^{5}-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =32{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =32{[{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =32({sin}^{3}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{sin}^{3}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =32(1-0) \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
